OL,3,GNEWSAWoman to be reunited with
OL,4,A'much-loved' dog's ashes which lay in
OL,5,Alost property for months
OL,6,
OL,7,FA bereaved pet owner will be reunited
OL,8,Fwith her "much-loved" dog's ashes after
OL,9,Fthey lay in ScotRail's lost property
OL,10,Ffor months.
OL,12,FThe woman had accidentally left the
OL,13,Funusual urn, which was wrapped in the
OL,14,Farms of a teddy bear, on a train when
OL,15,Fshe got off the LNER service in
OL,16,FEdinburgh in May. The train continued
OL,17,Fon to Aberdeen where the urn was handed
OL,18,Fto station staff.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
